Privacy Policy for Go aura

Last Updated: July 24, 2026

This Privacy Policy explains how Go aura, developed by Abdullah Ali, handles user information.

1. Information Collection

Go aura does not collect, store, transmit, or share personal information.

The app does not require users to create an account or provide information such as:

* Name
* Email address
* Phone number
* Location
* Photos
* Contacts
* Device identifiers
* Health or fitness information

2. Tracking

Go aura does not track users across apps, websites, or services.

The app does not use advertising identifiers, cookies, tracking technologies, or user profiling tools.

3. Analytics

Go aura does not use analytics services and does not collect information about how users interact with the app.

4. Advertising

Go aura does not display advertisements and does not use third-party advertising networks or advertising services.

5. Data Storage

Any settings, preferences, or progress created within Go aura are stored locally on the user’s device.

This information is not transmitted to the developer and is not stored on external servers or cloud services.

Deleting the app may permanently remove locally stored information.

6. Third-Party Services

Go aura does not share user information with third parties and does not use third-party services that collect personal information.

7. Children’s Privacy

Go aura does not knowingly collect personal information from children or any other users.

Because the app does not collect personal data, no personal information relating to children is stored or processed.

8. Data Security

Because Go aura does not collect or transmit personal information, no personal user data is stored on the developer’s servers.

Users are responsible for maintaining the security of their own devices.

9. Changes to This Privacy Policy

This Privacy Policy may be updated if the app’s features or privacy practices change.

Any changes will be published on this page with an updated revision date.

